config DRM_TSI_SKYLP_VB
	tristate "TSI SkyLP video bridge register core" if KUNIT
	depends on DRM
	help
	  Register encoding and programming sequences for the SkyLP video
	  bridge: mode-to-timing conversion, framebuffer address and format
	  programming, channel start and stop, and interrupt acknowledge.
	  They are kept free of DRM object state so they can be unit tested
	  on their own. The prompt only appears in KUnit builds.

config DRM_TSI_SKYLP_KUNIT_TEST
	tristate "KUnit tests for the TSI SkyLP video bridge core" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on DRM_TSI_SKYLP_VB && KUNIT
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Unit tests for the video bridge programming core. They cover mode
	  to timing conversion and its field limits, the accepted pixel
	  formats, the 40-bit and 4 GiB scanout address rules, page-flip
	  slot alternation and write order, and the interrupt acknowledge
	  sequence. They run against a fake register file.

	  If unsure, say N.
